<article class="env-lemma" id="213C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/213C">Lemma <span data-tag="213C">5.3.2.6</span>.</a> Let $\calB ' \rightarrow \calB $ be a Cartesian fibration. Suppose that $\calB $ has an initial object $B$ and that $\calB '$ is filtered. Then the fiber $\calB '_{B} = \calB ' \times _{\calB } \{ B\} $ is a contractible Kan complex. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $B$ is an initial object of $\calB $, the inclusion $\{  B\} ^{op} \subseteq \calB ^{op}$ is cofinal. Proposition <a href="/tag/458D" data-tag="458D">4.1.2.14</a> implies that the inclusion $(\calB '_{B})^{op} \subseteq (\calB ')^{op}$ is also cofinal, and therefore a weak homotopy equivalence. It now suffices to prove that $\calB '$ is weakly contractible, which follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/E4A7" data-tag="E4A7">5.3.1.18</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>